{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PZw2QrHdhz2QzFTYsegajf","type":"tool_result","content":"655:## 24. The base-AR window times the governor, not the engine — and it is 21 % (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n692:## 25. A unit gate that stops six times short of the regime it is quoted about (ladder 1.9, 2026-08-20)\n721:## 26. A field that was never computed compares equal, and equal reads as exonerated (ladder 1.9)\n749:## 27. `build/decode` and `dsv4-server` do not share a prefill, and a bit-exactness result on one says nothing about the other (ladder 1.9)\n770:## 28. A tuning default that was a regression at its own design point, and the mechanism story that was wrong (ladder 1.7, 2026-08-20)\n814:## 29. A dprof mark that timed another stream's work, and reported it as a 3.2x swing in a GEMM (ladder 1.8, 2026-08-20)\n880:## 30. A two-arm gate sweep in which the arms were identical by construction (ladder 1b.2, 2026-08-20)\n909:## 31. The resident-set line cannot price a cache that has not been touched (ladder 1b.2, 2026-08-20)\n939:## 32. The first pass through the arena reads scratch it never wrote, so run 1 of a process disagrees with every later run (ladder 1.11, 2026-08-20)\n974:## 33. Pairing does not remove a between-load offset — one arm order could not resolve a 0.9 ms effect, and two could (ladder 1.11, 2026-08-20)\n1020:## 34. The arm switch never switched, and the tell was that the null was *too* clean (ladder 1.12, 2026-08-20)\n1069:## 35. A byte-identity gate run past the length at which the engine is not byte-identical (ladder 1.12, 2026-08-20)\n=== kernel-opt ===\n74:## 2. Structural wins\n76:### 2.1 Full-step CUDA graph (F44)\n85:### 2.2 The arena (F44, F83)\n100:### 2.3 Adaptive verify width (F49, F59, F63)\n109:### 2.4 Fork/join the kv chain (F57)\n138:### 2.5 Don't recompute a prefix that cannot have changed — cache the main-KV (ladder 1.0, 2026-08-20)\n237:### 2.6 A selection sort is not a top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n348:### 2.7 Change which kernel the bit-exactness claim is *against* — `index_score` as a register-tiled GEMM (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n420:### 2.8 The one adopted win that is not a kernel — actually serve the head you trained (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)\n447:### 2.9 `sparse_attn` — stage the gathered row in shared memory, and vectorise the load without losing bit-exactness (ladder 1.7, 2026-08-20)\n522:### 2.10 Join a side stream where the data is needed, not where it was forked (ladder 1.11, 2026-08-20)\n569:### 2.11 One warp, a 2-D tile — `gemm_fp32` at the compressor emit (ladder 1.12, 2026-08-20)\n652:## 3. Precision and layout\n685:## 4. What every adopted change has in common\n=== negresults ===\n119:## 4c. Adopted, bit-exact, and worth nothing — the `lim <= topk` early-out (ladder 1.3, 2026-08-20)\n154:## 4d. Superseded before it shipped — the tiled `index_score`, and the cost of picking the wrong reference (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n195:## 4e. The lever that was already applied — `jetson_clocks` (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n242:## 4f. Two hypotheses killed on the way to localising the prefill race (ladder 1.9, 2026-08-20)\n270:## 4g. Retired on a null before it was built on — `hpb` alone, and the reuse hypothesis (ladder 1.7, 2026-08-20)\n301:## 4h. Headroom that was never there — the `cattn:q_proj` \"free 4.4 ms\" (ladder 1.8, 2026-08-20)\n330:## 4i. Packing the KV cache is a CAPACITY lever, not a throughput one — and the kernel it feeds says why (ladder 1b.2, 2026-08-20)\n388:## 5. What the negatives taught","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17d5ee56-c565-4475-a9f8-4b3d4b9993e5","uuid":"d17d6a68-d1b0-4621-ac48-eef0403318a9","timestamp":"2026-08-21T04:11:03.634Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"655:## 24. The base-AR window times the governor, not the engine — and it is 21 % (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n692:## 25. A unit gate that stops six times short of the regime it is quoted about (ladder 1.9, 2026-08-20)\