{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeFHhqYgr25NgkMp2Lt3m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NGGBakuYgAHC7AjTGN1Rdi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; cat > tools/genout_within.py <<'PYEOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"genout_within.py — ladder 1.10. Does ONE process reproduce ITSELF on a repeated sweep point?\n\n`genout_compare.py` compares two DSV4_GENOUT files, which means two processes and therefore two\n100.40 GiB checkpoint loads. On this box that is the expensive and the FRAGILE way to ask the\nquestion -- 1.10's first two attempts at it lost an arm to the memguard at MemAvailable 1.0 GB,\nbecause 100.40 GiB of weights in a 122.8 GiB pool leaves the loader ~7 GiB of headroom and the\nmemguard also fires on the fall RATE. It is also the WEAKER question: two loads differ in their\nallocator state, so \"the two files differ\" has an answer that is not about the computation.\n\nPoint the sweep at the SAME prompt several times in ONE process and every pair is exactly the same\ninput on exactly the same state. 1.0's original observation is in this form -- \"identical points\ngive different token sequences\" -- so this is the instrument that observation deserved.\n\n  python3 tools/genout_within.py <genout.txt> [<label>=<n_repeats> ...]\n\nWith no grouping argument, points are grouped by their PROMPT PREFIX: two lines whose ids agree up\nto the shorter one's generated region belong to the same repeat group. Exit 0 iff every pair inside\nevery group is identical at every position.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys, collections, itertools\n\n\ndef main(argv):\n    path = argv[0]\n    lines = [l.strip() for l in open(path) if l.strip()]\n    pts = [[int(x) for x in l.split(\",\")] for l in lines]\n    if not pts:\n        print(f\"MALFORMED: {path} has no points\"); return 2\n\n    # Group by prompt. The prompt length is not recorded in the file, so use the longest common\n    # prefix as the key: repeats of one sweep point share their whole prompt by construction, and\n    # two DIFFERENT prompts of this suite differ within their first few ids.\n    groups = collections.defaultdict(list)\n    for i, p in enumerate(pts):\n        groups[tuple(p[:8])].append(i)\n\n    print(f\"{path}: {len(pts)} point(s) in {len(groups)} repeat group(s)\")\n    bad = 0\n    for k, idxs in groups.items():\n        n = len(idxs)\n        if n < 2:\n            print(f\"  group {k[:4]}...: only one point, nothing to compare within\"); continue\n        npairs = 0; ndiff = 0; firsts = []\n        for a, b in itertools.combinations(idxs, 2):\n            npairs += 1\n            pa, pb = pts[a], pts[b]\n            m = min(len(pa), len(pb))\n            first = next((i for i in range(m) if pa[i] != pb[i]), None)\n            if first is None and len(pa) != len(pb): first = m\n            if first is not None:\n                ndiff += 1; firsts.append(first)\n        bad += ndiff\n        lens = {len(pts[i]) for i in idxs}\n        note = f\"first divergence at position(s) {sorted(set(firsts))}\" if firsts else \"identical at every position\"\n        print(f\"  group of {n} repeats (len {sorted(lens)}): {ndiff}/{npairs} pairs differ -- {note}\")\n    print(\"VERDICT: \" + (\"the process DOES NOT reproduce itself\" if bad else\n                         \"every repeat of every point is byte-identical\"))\n    return 1 if bad else 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) < 2: print(__doc__); sys.exit(2)\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))\nPYEOF\npython3 tools/genout_within.py evidence/decode_loop/genout_1p9_R1.txt","description":"Write within-process genout comparator and smoke-test it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2721,"cache_read_input_tokens":248735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h