{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeFN68SWosKUKhFr6UZ3N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A82YMmMJvH1BFABC77gyXv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; cat > /tmp/kopt212.md <<'EOF'\n\n### 2.12 The kernel that read the buffer it was writing — `hadamard`, staged through shared memory (ladder 1.10, 2026-08-21)\n\n**This is the one adopted change on this page whose measured gain is CORRECTNESS, and it is here so\nthat nobody optimises the staging back out.** `build/decode`'s prefill had not reproduced itself\nabove ~163 positions since the indexer was written; it does now, at every length. The speed effect\nis a measured null and is stated as one below.\n\n**Mechanism.** `hadamard_kernel` computed `y[r,j] = D^-0.5 * Σ_i x[r,i] * (-1)^popcount(i&j)` with\none thread per `(r, j)`:\n\n```c\nfor (int i = 0; i < D; ++i) acc += (__popc(i & j) & 1) ? -xr[i] : xr[i];   // reads the WHOLE row\ny[idx] = acc * scale;                                                      // writes ONE of it\n```\n\nEvery thread of a row reads all `D` elements and overwrites one. That is correct exactly while\n`y != x` — and `kernels/compressor.cu`'s `rotate` branch called it `hadamard(out, out, groups, d)`,\nwith two more aliased sites in the decode emits. There is no in-place form of this transform: the\ndirect `O(D²)` evaluation needs the whole input row after some of it has been overwritten. The fix\ngives **one block one row**, stages the row into shared memory, `__syncthreads()`, and reduces out of\nshared, so the read set is closed before the write set opens.\n\n**Why it is bit-identical wherever it was already correct.** The sum is still serial in\n`i = 0..D-1` over the same values; only where the values *come from* changed. `gate_hadamard_alias`\nproves it directly: with `y != x`, the staged kernel reproduces the flat kernel bit for bit,\n**200/200 repeats at all 21 row counts, on both arms**, and `gate_units` still passes the hadamard\ngolden. That negative control is what makes the positive result attributable.\n\n**Measured gain, kernel level** (`gate_hadamard_alias --bench`, 200 iterations, D = 128):\n\n| rows | 1 | 64 | 256 | 384 | 768 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| where | both aliased emit sites | q-side, per verify | prefill s=1,024 | q-side at K=6 | prefill s=3,072 |\n| flat / staged | **1.49×** | 1.06× | 1.14× | 0.99× | 0.99× |\n\nD global loads per thread become D shared loads per thread plus D/blockDim global loads per *block*,\nwhich is why the small shapes gain and the large ones — already L1-resident — do not.\n\n**Measured gain, engine level: __BAND__** That is the honest answer and it was pre-registered as the\nexpected one. `hadamard` runs ~63 times per forward at rows ∈ {1, 64, ≤384}, totalling a few tens of\nmicroseconds of a ~130 ms forward; the kernel-level table above bounds the whole effect at ~0.1\nms/forward, an order of magnitude below the 3.5 % run-to-run spread. **A kernel that is 0.1 % of the\nforward cannot be measured end to end, and reporting the band rather than the ratio is the only way\nto say so.**\n\n**The gates.** `tests/gate_hadamard_alias.cu` runs both arms in ONE process via\n`hadamard_set_stage()` — same binary, same input, one dispatch different — sweeps rows across the\nboundary at 200 repeats each, and **returns non-zero if the OFF arm ever stops reproducing the\ndefect**, because a gate that can no longer see its own bug is not a passing gate. `--control` flips\none ulp in the reference and requires every comparison on both arms to see it. Then the engine:\n`scripts/lhash_verify.sh` re-runs 1.9's R and W protocols (0/56 pairs and 0/8 lengths, against\n56/56 and 2/8 before) and `scripts/genout_within_run.sh` runs four identical points at ctx 1,023 ×\n256 generated tokens inside one process on both arms — **6/6 pairs diverge with\n`DSV4_HADAMARD_STAGE=0`, first at generated token 26/42/45; 0/6 with it unset.**\n\n**What it does NOT retract.** `dsv4-server` prefills in `EXT_CHUNK` = 64-row chunks through\n`cblock_verify_step`, so it never issued `rows > 1` and never raced. Every server number on this\npage stands. [`measurement-and-traps.md` §36](measurement-and-traps.md),\n[`negative-results.md` §4j](negative-results.md).\nEOF\nwc -l /tmp/kopt212.md; tail -2 evidence/decode_loop/hadamard_ab.log","description":"Draft kernel-optimisations 2.12"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1212,"cache_read_input_tokens":298510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1212},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17d5ee56-c565-4475-a9f8-4b3d4b9993e5","uuid":"3fb37b5f-3366-45df-802f-3d10d34ec18c","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:46:16.159Z","request_id":"req_011CeFN66fMSWmb22BhuZzpe"}
