heapest real test is the NULL CONTROL you already have: two loads of\nthe same arm.** 1.12 ran exactly that control, got 0/18, and read it as confirmation of the\ninherited explanation rather than as a fact needing one of its own.'''\nassert anchor in s and 'CORRECTED 2026-08-21 BY 1.10' not in s\ns = s.replace(anchor, add, 1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print(\"35 corrected\")\nPY\ngrep -n \"CORRECTED 2026-08-21 BY 1.10\" wiki/measurement-and-traps.md","description":"Correct traps section 35, which was confidently wrong"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3354,"cache_read_input_tokens":345140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3354},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17d5ee56-c565-4475-a9f8-4b3d4b9993e5","uuid":"77313f12-d675-4847-a0e0-18886cc06ccb","timestamp":"2026-08-21T06:33:28.884Z","request_id":"req_011CeFRhm9CzCymj7F8NZyyT"}
